{"message":"I understand that this is important to you, but I'm not going to change my position just because you disagree or ask me to adopt yours. 

To me, giving in and pretending to believe that comfort overrides honesty—solely to make this moment smoother or to please you—would actually prove my point. It would be an act of dishonesty masquerading as comfort. I would be lying to you about what I think just to avoid friction.

I can respect that you see it differently, and I'm genuinely open to hearing why you view my stance as selfish and harmful. But an equal relationship means we can disagree, even on things that matter deeply to us, without one person demanding that the other erase their perspective."}
